The Relic is a 1997 American monster-horror film directed by Peter Hyams and based on
the best-selling 1995 novel Relic by Douglas Preston and Lincoln Child.

11
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:06,000
The film stars Penelope Ann Miller, Tom Sizemore,
Linda Hunt, and James Whitmore.

12
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
In the film, a detective and a biologist try to defeat a South American monstrous reptilian
creature which is on a killing spree in the Field Museum of Natural History in Chicago.

13
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:06,000
The movie was shot in Chicago at the Field Museum of Natural History.

14
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
Production was originally intended to be held at the American
Museum of Natural History in New York City.

15
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
However, a deal could not be reached and, after taking interest in the film's
premise, the Field Museum offered to let the studio shoot there instead.

16
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
The film was the second on-screen collaboration between Hunt, Miller, and supporting actor
Chi Muoi Lo, all three of whom also worked on the film Kindergarten Cop.

17
01:25:00,000 --> 01:25:06,000
The film was released in the United States on
January 10, 1997, by Paramount Pictures.

18
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:06,000
It grossed only $48 million worldwide against a $40–60 million budget.

19
01:35:00,000 --> 01:35:06,000
It was the last film appearance of actress Audra Lindley.

